<ResourceDictionary xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

  <!--
    Fluent 2 Premium Theme pass: no longer self-merges Colors.xaml (for
    Rojan.Effect.FocusGlow's Accent color below) - see Themes/Controls.xaml's
    own doc comment for why.

    Phase 16: raw shadow building blocks, one per Fluent 2 depth level
    (2/4/8/16 - Fluent's own ambient-shadow scale, minus the very top
    "64" tier this app has no use for). Neutral black shadows, not
    color-tinted ones - depth comes from elevation now, not from a
    saturated glow on every surface (that's what the old
    Rojan.Effect.ElevationMedium/GlowAccent pair did, tinted with the
    brand purple). Available for a one-off custom effect; Controls.xaml/
    ShellChrome.xaml consume Elevation.xaml's semantic tier names instead
    (Rojan.Effect.ElevationCard etc.), which redeclare these same depth
    values under a "what is this surface" name rather than a "how deep"
    one - WPF resource dictionaries have no cheap alias mechanism for a
    Freezable like DropShadowEffect, so the two files' values
    intentionally match rather than one referencing the other.

    Fluent 2 Premium Theme pass: opacities lowered (0.24/0.28/0.32/0.4 ->
    0.10/0.12/0.16/0.22) to match real Fluent 2's genuinely soft ambient
    shadows - the prior values read as a much heavier, dark-theme-era
    "film noir" depth effect once seen on Light.xaml's warm, near-white
    surfaces; ShadowDepth/BlurRadius (the actual size/spread of each
    tier) are unchanged, only how dark the shadow itself is.
  -->

  <DropShadowEffect x:Key="Rojan.Effect.ShadowLevel2"
                     Color="Black"
                     Direction="270"
                     ShadowDepth="1"
                     BlurRadius="4"
                     Opacity="0.10" />

  <DropShadowEffect x:Key="Rojan.Effect.ShadowLevel4"
                     Color="Black"
                     Direction="270"
                     ShadowDepth="2"
                     BlurRadius="8"
                     Opacity="0.12" />

  <DropShadowEffect x:Key="Rojan.Effect.ShadowLevel8"
                     Color="Black"
                     Direction="270"
                     ShadowDepth="4"
                     BlurRadius="16"
                     Opacity="0.16" />

  <DropShadowEffect x:Key="Rojan.Effect.ShadowLevel16"
                     Color="Black"
                     Direction="270"
                     ShadowDepth="6"
                     BlurRadius="28"
                     Opacity="0.22" />

  <!--
    Accent-tinted glow - deliberately kept separate from the neutral
    elevation shadows above. Used only for the rare interactive-highlight
    moment (a hovered primary button), never as a substitute for
    elevation, consistent with "accent color used sparingly."
  -->
  <DropShadowEffect x:Key="Rojan.Effect.FocusGlow"
                     Color="{StaticResource Rojan.Color.Accent}"
                     Direction="0"
                     ShadowDepth="0"
                     BlurRadius="12"
                     Opacity="0.55" />

</ResourceDictionary>
